@startuml
|Primary CDN Web Server (WS)|
start
:Monitor load / detect hotspot (flash crowd);
if (Exceptional load spike?) then (yes)
  :Initiate peering trigger request;
  |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
  :Receive initialization request;
  :Assess expected & unexpected load increase;
  :Generate service requirements\n(based on current circumstances and customer SLAs);

  |Service Registry (SR)|
  :Provide local resource/service/access information;

  |Policy Repository (PR)|
  :Provide SLAs and policies\n(visibility/privacy constraints, peering policies);

  |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
  :Create/Update negotiated relationship terms\n(legal/financial/technical SLA terms,\nregion preference, duration, penalties, preconditions);
  :Identify roles/activities for coordination/cooperation;

  |Peering Agent (PA - Primary CDN)|
  :Receive service requirements from Mediator;
  :Discover potential peer CDNs\n(predict performance; handle limited info sharing);

  if (Preexisting long-term peering arrangement found?) then (yes)
    :Return existing peering arrangement candidates;
  else (no)
    :Perform short-term negotiations with target peer PAs;
  endif

  if (Any peer CDN interested / resources offered?) then (yes)
    |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
    :Select peer(s) and confirm negotiated relationship;

    fork
      |Peering Agent (PA - Primary CDN)|
      :Configure CDN peering protocols at conduit/gateway;
      :Advertise configurations via inter-PA communication\n(topology, geo proximity, capability, performance);
    fork again
      |Policy Repository (PR)|
      :Deploy/virtualize peering arrangement policies\n(P_WS, P_M, P_Peering and delegated policies);
      :Provide rules for access control and administration;
    end fork

    |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
    :Establish peering arrangement;
    :Create/Update SR instance encapsulating\nlocal + delegated external resources;

    |SLA Allocator (Primary CDN)|
    :Provision/reserve WS resources\nfor local and delegated SLAs;
    :Enforce SLA terms;

    |Primary CDN Web Services Host / WSs|
    :Serve end-users per negotiated policies;
    :Perform on-demand caching/content selection/routing;

    |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
    :Control traffic redirection to peer WSs\n(what portion of requests, what content replicated,\nreplication decision and policies);
    :Assist request assignment/redirection\n(DNS updates via PAs; gateway redirection; intra-cluster redirection);

    fork
      |CDN Gateways (M/PA/PR as conceptual gateway)|
      :Measure and aggregate load information\n(periodic or threshold-based);
      :Exchange aggregated load info with peer gateways;
    fork again
      |Participating CDNs|
      :Cooperative pull-based content replication\n(subject to contributed resources);
    fork again
      |Participating CDNs|
      :Exchange accounting information for billing\n(based on negotiated relationship);
    end fork

    |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
    if (Need disband or re-arrange?) then (yes)
      if (Circumstances no longer hold\nOR peering not beneficial\nOR need expansion for additional load\nOR contributions not met?) then (yes)
        :Disband or re-arrange within negotiated relationship scope;
        if (Re-arrangement requires more resources?) then (yes)
          :Tune service requirements / negotiated terms;
          -> :Identify roles/activities for coordination/cooperation;
        else (no)
          stop
        endif
      else (no)
        stop
      endif
    else (no)
      stop
    endif

  else (no)
    |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
    :No suitable peer found / no interest;
    repeat
      :Reconsider service requirements;
      :Tune negotiated relationship terms/policies;
      |Peering Agent (PA - Primary CDN)|
      :Retry resource discovery / negotiations with peer PAs;
    repeat while (Still no peer interested?) is (yes)
    |Mediator (Primary CDN)|
    :Proceed with established peer(s) after successful retry;
    stop
  endif

else (no)
  :Continue normal content delivery locally;
  stop
endif
@enduml